                "retweet_count": 969,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "We should not be made to continue flooding health insurance companies with taxpayer dollars under Obamacare as the price to open up the government.\n\u00a0\nI find Senator Schumer\u2019s demands ridiculous and equivalent to political hostage taking to continue bad policy.\n\u00a0\nUnder Obamacare, health insurance companies\u2019 average weighted stock prices have exploded \u2013 a more than 1000% increase \u2013 because they\u2019re the biggest winners of Obamacare. In 2010, President Obama promised that healthcare premiums would go down by $2500 per family. To the contrary, from 2013-2019 premiums under Obamacare increased over 100% with no end in sight.\n\u00a0\nTherefore, my no vote will be an unequivocal rejection of Senator Schumer\u2019s very bad idea.",
